        "quotes": [
          {
            "char_start": 697582,
            "char_end": 698803,
            "line_start": 15978,
            "line_end": 16023,
            "quote": "\"id\": \"MEC-01\",\n      \"name\": \"SCALAR_MULTIPLICATIVE_ACTION\",\n      \"canonical\": \"S_c(x)=c x, c>0\",\n      \"members\": [\n        {\n          \"system\": \"SUN scalar kernel\",\n          \"objects\": [\n            \"R=2/3\",\n            \"L=3/4\",\n            \"O=RL=1/2\"\n          ],\n          \"relation\": \"NATIVE\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"system\": \"sanfen sunyi\",\n          \"objects\": [\n            \"D=2/3\",\n            \"U=4/3\"\n          ],\n          \"relation\": \"EXACT_GENERATOR_FAMILY_EQUIVALENCE to SUN on positive scalar carrier\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"system\": \"Zhu equal division\",\n          \"objects\": [\n            \"q=2^(1/12)\"\n          ],\n          \"relation\": \"ROOT_EXTENSION / SAME OPERATION FORM, NOT SAME SUBGROUP\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"system\": \"Messiaen augmentation/diminution\",\n          \"objects\": [\n            \"duration scaling c and c^-1\"\n          ],\n          \"relation\": \"SAME OPERATION FORM, DIFFERENT CARRIER/SEMANTICS\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"proved_relations\": [\n        \"<R,L> = {2^a 3^b} \\u2245 Z^2\",\n        \"sanfen D=R and U=L^-1\",\n        \"q not in <R,L> but q^12=2\",\n        \"O=RL is constructible\"\n      ],\n      \"status\": \"FROZEN_EQUIVALENCE_CLASS\"\n    },\n    {\n      ",
            "quote_sha256": "39248b8dba24ed608140d7ef2595c9d64b968b62fd0ad6d979ddf743db51fcff"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "32709e8763ac228cadc7cf5ef11c73eca6ada4257030855cc343ed4279474097",
        "path": "data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/SUN_DEEP_RECOVERY/SUN_Chinese_Lu_Depth_Pilot_2026-09-28.md",
        "sha256": "66e5d2d763e55411993bfcf4ad07ca4cc0a708f624264e226abf51b90531e9dd",
        "source_status": "source-bounded ideal pipe model; native order and physical idealization explicit",
        "quotes": [
          {
            "char_start": 5402,
            "char_end": 6476,
            "line_start": 49,
            "line_end": 54,
            "quote": "Let an ideal reference pipe have length `L₀`. CN-C03's first operation gives `L₁ = (2/3)L₀`. Its second operation gives `L₂ = (4/3)L₁ = (8/9)L₀`. Under the *idealized* inverse length–frequency relation, their frequency ratios against the reference are `3/2` and `9/8`. The second value follows from the **ordered path**; endpoint equality alone would not preserve the sequence or the pipe identities. This is a DERIVED computation from CN-C03, not a new historical source claim.\n\nFive tone positions and twelve lü form two address axes in CN-S03's formalization. Their product yields 60 ordered set-position contexts in that model. It does **not** establish 60 historical pipes, 60 empirically attested modes, or a universal Chinese count. The `T` and `t` actions have different preserved coordinates; an implementation must retain both.\n\nThe twelve-pipe generation, five-position function, and eight-material classification are separate structures. A single unlabeled “Chinese music number” node would erase their relation types and falsely imply a shared generation law.\n\n",
            "quote_sha256": "b017516c8905ac8b011f15b7a380e703c0db837cfcb4907c45def37ac8d2a028"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "7d5a026c9df7d3fdf06382c966729a7cf3da22dbc4a1276c9f809f7a139ce965",
        "path": "data/raw/reconstruction-recovered/73b3171aa010c78121f2d7798011ce36f6e4891f4ef1409d25ed98aaca16fcfc/ChatGPT-Comparative Research Protocol-20261030-1502.md",
        "sha256": "73b3171aa010c78121f2d7798011ce36f6e4891f4ef1409d25ed98aaca16fcfc",
        "source_status": "assistant acknowledgment of already established research, subsequent to direct user correction",
        "quotes": [
          {
            "char_start": 703384,
            "char_end": 703885,
            "line_start": 13742,
            "line_end": 13743,
            "quote": "**1\\. The Chinese-Western musical bridge was already established.** The reciprocal $2/3$, $4/3$, and $3/4$ relationships, Chinese pitch generation, the Western harmonic realization, and the Fludd-Kepler monochord bridge belong to the existing SUN foundation. They are not new validation results. The full bridge also includes the $81/80$ comma relationship and the $16/15$ boundary excursion. I should have used those together rather than repeatedly presenting the first three ratios as discoveries.\n\n",
            "quote_sha256": "b382df7ac853238ee79e42f01ce1a55a4683eeca60e781d88496ac62c6cbd50c"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "dd5004b2224cfaa99969f817c12d758ea41d503d4c93e8c680f681b001db7a77",
        "path": "data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/RELATED_LINEAGES/SUN_AUTHORITATIVE_MUTATION_CHRONOLOGY_2026-10-01.txt",
        "sha256": "def5acfb2239f58fe91efbdab0096feba38a6d3e0a18a9ca20bf1e0e950dff94",
        "source_status": "recovered equation/bridge chronology; source-specific lifted FK formalism",
        "quotes": [
          {
            "char_start": 13417,
            "char_end": 14032,
            "line_start": 822,
            "line_end": 889,
            "quote": "Composition is\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n(a,m)\\star(b,n)\r\n=\r\n(ab,m+n)\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nwith physical realization\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n\\Phi(a,m)=a\\,2^{-m}.\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nFor the FK loop\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\gamma_{\\rm FK}\r\n=\r\ne_{\\rm out}e_{\\rm return},\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nwe obtain\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n(r,\\delta)(\\gamma_{\\rm FK})\r\n=\r\n\\left(\r\n\\frac{16}{15},0\r\n\\right)\r\n\\star\r\n\\left(\r\n\\frac{15}{16},1\r\n\\right)\r\n=\r\n(1,1).\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nTherefore\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n\\Phi(1,1)=\\frac12.\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nThe local harmonic ratios close:\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n\\frac{16}{15}\\frac{15}{16}=1,\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\nwhile the generation/register coordinate advances:\r\n\r\n\\[\r\n\\boxed{\r\n\\delta_{\\rm loop}=1.\r\n}\r\n\\]\r\n\r\n",
            "quote_sha256": "b00cb9f168244c03c4ffe97e8582aefd1bf138c8c4349faca8917b6901a8b36d"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "6d0e6405bba76f693e8810327a39c0a663813316222c64fc4cc179a54f377fe9",
        "path": "data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/RELATED_LINEAGES/TOL_COMPLETE_WORK_ARCHIVE_2026-09-29 (1).md",
        "sha256": "1e471374598497383adaf7d6ab21af2dfb2a6999a0a41ae1f253072ddaf4f065",
        "source_status": "recovered TOL history/evaluation quotient; no named A/B maps invented",
        "quotes": [
          {
            "char_start": 13788,
            "char_end": 14374,
            "line_start": 698,
            "line_end": 745,
            "quote": "## 14. Unevaluated versus evaluated harmonic spaces\n\nTo preserve operation order/history, the harmonic IR was split:\n\n\\[\n\\widetilde{\\mathcal H}\n\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n\\mathcal H.\n\\]\n\nAn evaluation quotient:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nq_H=\\operatorname{eval}:\n\\widetilde{\\mathcal H}\n\\rightarrow\n\\mathcal H\n}\n\\]\n\npermits:\n\n\\[\nRL\\neq LR\n\\quad\\text{in }\\widetilde{\\mathcal H}\n\\]\n\nwhile:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\operatorname{eval}(RL)\n=\n\\operatorname{eval}(LR)\n=\n\\operatorname{eval}(O)\n=\n\\frac12\n}\n\\]\n\nin the evaluated harmonic space.\n\nThis is the harmonic-specific version of history-aware projected confluence.\n\n---\n\n",
            "quote_sha256": "adf4e05246014f4515af33b9850a68e519f8ca776a82274ec395a8d11588c930"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "8ad7da0f6595b714fa87a52b5da6803200b6eee38cb09c7f81c6cf907624f756",
        "path": "data/raw/archive/SUN_Universal_Archive/Library/SUN_DEEP_RECOVERY/SUN_Fludd_Kepler_Bridge_Registration_FREEZE_v0.1.md",
        "sha256": "f1c0e211ca729997638b5b53b19159147f4f8b3d71be6dc28293e73897c7114d",
        "source_status": "bridge-specific frozen hypothesis, including unresolved assembly/registration boundary",
        "quotes": [
          {
            "char_start": 244,
            "char_end": 884,
            "line_start": 6,
            "line_end": 49,
            "quote": "## Frozen registration hypothesis\n\nLet\n\n\\[\nQ_{FK}=\n\\bigl(\n\\{\\mathrm{MI},\\mathrm{FA}\\},\n\\{e_{\\rm out},e_{\\rm return}\\}\n\\bigr)\n\\]\n\nwith\n\n\\[\ne_{\\rm out}:\\mathrm{MI}\\to\\mathrm{FA},\n\\qquad\ne_{\\rm return}:\\mathrm{FA}\\to\\mathrm{MI},\n\\qquad\ne_{\\rm return}\\neq \\bar e_{\\rm out}.\n\\]\n\nDefine the native Kepler loop\n\n\\[\n\\gamma_{FK}=e_{\\rm out}e_{\\rm return}.\n\\]\n\nThe single unresolved bridge-specific registration is frozen as\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\operatorname{Mon}([\\gamma_{FK}])=D\n}\n\\]\n\nwhere\n\n\\[\nD(p,k)=(p,k+1).\n\\]\n\nEquivalently: completion of the source-native Kepler MI→FA→MI return loop is hypothesized to carry the Fluddian octave/register transition.\n\n",
            "quote_sha256": "406a5d7c0f652d82635c3c0e6700c8e0fb28e6aa89b1260ffc9e54f461f75fd0"
          },
          {
            "char_start": 884,
            "char_end": 3640,
            "line_start": 50,
            "line_end": 107,
            "quote": "## Evidence-status decomposition\n\n| Component | Status |\n|---|---|\n| \\(MI\\to FA\\to MI\\) ordered excursion | SOURCE-ATTESTED / NATIVE |\n| FA as the distinct intermediate pitch-class state | SOURCE-ATTESTED |\n| Exactly one modeled transient FA state | MINIMAL FAITHFUL REALIZATION, conditional on no unattested hidden states |\n| Distinct outbound and return channels | CONDITIONALLY DERIVED for nontrivial path-history/monodromy |\n| \\(e_{\\rm return}\\neq \\bar e_{\\rm out}\\) | MATHEMATICALLY REQUIRED for the chosen nontrivial-monodromy representation |\n| \\(\\rho=16/15\\) | DERIVED under frozen comma/enclosure constraints |\n| Total grade \\(+1\\) | CONDITIONALLY DERIVED from frozen \\(\\Phi\\), local cancellation, integer grade, and half-scale endpoint |\n| Boundary timing at \\(C_3\\) | CONDITIONALLY DERIVED from ten-visible capacity + ordinary sibling persistence |\n| Fludd typed lower/material/generative vs upper/formal/regenerative boundary | SOURCE-ATTESTED |\n| Fludd octave/register junction at that boundary | SOURCE-ATTESTED |\n| \\(\\operatorname{Mon}([\\gamma_{FK}])=D\\) | REMAINING ASSEMBLY / REGISTRATION HYPOTHESIS |\n| Full \\(B_{FK}\\) as universal SUN law | NOT ESTABLISHED |\n\n## What is no longer open\n\nThe project no longer treats the following as unexplained topology choices:\n\n1. why there is an MI→FA→MI return excursion;\n2. why FA is the native intermediate pitch-class state;\n3. why a nontrivial path-history model cannot collapse outward and return to one edge/inverse traversal;\n4. why the local scalar factor is \\(16/15\\) under the frozen enclosure;\n5. why the boundary must occur at \\(C_3\\), conditional on the ten-visible/persistence architecture.\n\n## Exact remaining claim\n\nThe first-edition evidence independently supplies:\n- exact comma correction;\n- returning MI→FA→MI motion;\n- typed Fludd boundary;\n- octave/register landing at that boundary.\n\nWhat it does **not** explicitly supply is the composition:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\text{Kepler returned MI}\n\\mapsto\n\\text{Fludd opposite octave/register sheet}.\n}\n\\]\n\nThat composition is the frozen bridge hypothesis.\n\n## Review / falsification trigger\n\nDo not reopen topology selection or numerical-constant search.\n\nReopen this freeze only if one of the following occurs:\n\n1. independent source/native evidence explicitly supports or contradicts the MI-return → Fludd-register assignment;\n2. an independently defined realization of the same native components yields a different register action while preserving all source-attested constraints;\n3. the two-channel monodromy model is shown to be mathematically inapplicable to the actual source-native state space.\n\nAbsent one of those triggers, the assembly remains a bridge-specific hypothesis and is not promoted into SUN's universal generative core.\n",
            "quote_sha256": "d8e6ea12dc43d8968d8aeaa3141812b203d944d9d609321c39d685f7ac894193"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
